                <pb facs="0796" n="510" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg510"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/2679</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-06-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 29, 1916</hi>
                        </date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received 5.30 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4507. My 3281,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d628-f1"/> November 25 and 2713,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d628-f2"/> December 20, <hi rendition="#italic">re</hi> shipment
                    tobacco to neutral consignees in neutral countries. Am to-day in receipt
                    circular from Foreign Office stating British Government unable continue policy
                    of permitting unrestricted importation tobacco into enemy countries and cannot
                    guarantee future continuance noninterference which they have hitherto extended
                    to such shipments. Copy circular follows in next pouch.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
